  "question": {
    "text": "A point charge of magnitude $+1 \\mu \\mathrm{C}$ is fixed at $(0$, $0,0)$. An isolated uncharged spherical conductor, is fixed with its center at $(4,0,0)$. The potential and the induced electric field at the centre of the sphere is :"
  },
  "options": [
    {
      "text": "\n$1.8 \\times 10^5 \\mathrm{~V}$ and $-5.625 \\times 10^6 \\mathrm{~V} / \\mathrm{m}$\n",
      "is_correct": false
    },
    {
      "text": "\n$0 \\mathrm{~V}$ and $0 \\mathrm{~V} / \\mathrm{m}$\n",
      "is_correct": false
    },
    {
      "text": "\n$2.25 \\times 10^5 \\mathrm{~V}$ and $-5.625 \\times 10^6 \\mathrm{~V} / \\mathrm{m}$\n",
      "is_correct": true
    },
    {
      "text": "\n$2.25 \\times 10^5 \\mathrm{~V}$ and $0 \\mathrm{~V} / \\mathrm{m}$",
      "is_correct": false
    }
  ],
  "correct_answer": [
    "C"
  ],
  "solution": {
    "text": "$\\mathrm{q}=1 \\mu \\mathrm{C}=1 \\times 10^{-6} \\mathrm{C}$\n$$\n\\mathrm{r}=4 \\mathrm{~cm}=4 \\times 10^{-2} \\mathrm{~m}\n$$\nPotential $\\mathrm{V}=\\frac{\\mathrm{kq}}{\\mathrm{r}}$\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n& =\\frac{9 \\times 10^9 \\times 10^{-6}}{4 \\times 10^{-2}} \\\\\n& =2.25 \\times 10^5 \\mathrm{~V} .\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\nInduced electric field $\\mathrm{E}=-\\frac{\\mathrm{kq}}{\\mathrm{r}^2}$\n$$\n=\\frac{9 \\times 10^9 \\times 1 \\times 10^{-6}}{16 \\times 10^{-4}}=-5.625 \\times 10^6 \\mathrm{~V} / \\mathrm{m}\n$$"
  }
}